   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **someday (1st time ever)** (1 other source): Someday was played live for the first time, and the band played it twice, joking it was so bad [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **right to the ways and the rules of the world**: back after 58 archived shows (585 days) [6]\n- **dont get too close 2 my fantasy**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **fancy pants**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [6]\n- **all things must pass (george harrison cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **if you can save yourself, you can save us all**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: someday (1st time ever), someday (2nd time ever) [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2002-02-21.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 28 songs; 130 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **Ween2002-02-21**: source not stated; 28 songs; 130 min [2]\n- **ween-2002-02-21.mk-4v.sxm-2.sbm-1.d-100**: source not stated; 0 songs; 141 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The whole show was acoustic [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2002-02-21.shnf**: taped by Bobby Bourbon; source: MK4V's-> SXM2-> SBM1(mod)-> D100 (front center table) [1]",
